body:
Summary: This PR adds Terraform module examples and security guidance for configuring the SIEM-ready audit export S3 sink for Redwood Inference (beta). It includes: (1) an opinionated S3 bucket + SSE-KMS setup suitable for audit log exports, (2) least-privilege IAM for the exporter writer identity, (3) a bucket policy that enforces TLS + encryption and blocks public access, (4) a KMS key policy that permits the exporter role to use the key without broad account-wide grants, and (5) notes for Private deployments on AWS networking (S3 Gateway Endpoint + KMS Interface Endpoint) to avoid public egress.

Motivation: Multiple beta customers asked for concrete, copy/pasteable infra examples for the S3 sink that align with SOC2/ISO expectations (encryption, access control, and evidence-ready policies). We also saw configuration drift in customer setups during onboarding (e.g., missing kms:ViaService constraints, exporter granted s3:*). This PR standardizes recommended patterns and documents trade-offs.

What’s included: - examples/siem_audit_export_s3/ (new): end-to-end example wiring a dedicated bucket, KMS key, and IAM role/policy for the audit-exporter writer. - modules/s3_audit_export_bucket/ (new): small helper module for creating a compliant export bucket (public access block, optional access logs, lifecycle). - docs/private-endpoints.md (new): notes for Private/VPC-only deployments on using VPC endpoints for S3 and KMS and verifying connectivity without opening internet egress. - docs/siem-audit-export-s3.md (updated): adds “policy rationale” sections and troubleshooting for AccessDenied / KMS.

Notable details / decisions: - Enforce SSE-KMS: The bucket policy requires x-amz-server-side-encryption=aws:kms and (optionally) a specific KMS key ARN via s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption-aws-kms-key-id. - Deny insecure transport: Deny any request where aws:SecureTransport is false. - Least-privilege S3: Exporter role is scoped to s3:PutObject, s3:AbortMultipartUpload, and s3:ListBucket (only for the target bucket/prefix). We explicitly avoid s3:GetObject and s3:DeleteObject in the example. - KMS permissions: Exporter role receives kms:Encrypt, kms:GenerateDataKey, kms:Decrypt is NOT required for writes but is included only when customers want the same role to validate reads; example shows a toggle and defaults to write-only. Includes kms:ViaService and kms:CallerAccount constraints to avoid key misuse outside S3.

Illustrative snippets (from examples/siem_audit_export_s3/main.tf):

1) S3 bucket policy (enforce TLS + SSE-KMS + no public access)

resource "aws_s3_bucket_policy" "audit_export" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.audit_export.id
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Sid      = "DenyInsecureTransport"
        Effect   = "Deny"
        Principal= "*"
        Action   = "s3:*"
        Resource = [
          aws_s3_bucket.audit_export.arn,
          "${aws_s3_bucket.audit_export.arn}/*"
        ]
        Condition = {
          Bool = { "aws:SecureTransport" = "false" }
        }
      },
      {
        Sid      = "DenyIncorrectEncryptionHeader"
        Effect   = "Deny"
        Principal= "*"
        Action   = "s3:PutObject"
        Resource = "${aws_s3_bucket.audit_export.arn}/*"
        Condition = {
          StringNotEquals = {
            "s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption" = "aws:kms"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        Sid      = "DenyUnEncryptedObjectUploads"
        Effect   = "Deny"
        Principal= "*"
        Action   = "s3:PutObject"
        Resource = "${aws_s3_bucket.audit_export.arn}/*"
        Condition = {
          Null = { "s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption" = "true" }
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

2) Exporter IAM policy (least privilege)

data "aws_iam_policy_document" "exporter_write" {
  statement {
    sid     = "WriteAuditExportObjects"
    actions = ["s3:PutObject", "s3:AbortMultipartUpload"]
    resources = ["${aws_s3_bucket.audit_export.arn}/${var.export_prefix}/*"]
  }
  statement {
    sid     = "ListBucketForPrefix"
    actions = ["s3:ListBucket"]
    resources = [aws_s3_bucket.audit_export.arn]
    condition {
      test     = "StringLike"
      variable = "s3:prefix"
      values   = ["${var.export_prefix}/*"]
    }
  }
}

3) KMS key policy constraints (S3-only usage)

statement {
  sid = "AllowExporterUseOfKeyViaS3"
  principals { type = "AWS" identifiers = [aws_iam_role.audit_exporter.arn] }
  actions = ["kms:Encrypt", "kms:GenerateDataKey"]
  resources = ["*"]
  condition {
    test     = "StringEquals"
    variable = "kms:ViaService"
    values   = ["s3.${data.aws_region.current.name}.amazonaws.com"]
  }
  condition {
    test     = "StringEquals"
    variable = "kms:CallerAccount"
    values   = [data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id]
  }
}

Private deployment notes (docs/private-endpoints.md): - S3 sink with no public egress: use a Gateway VPC Endpoint for com.amazonaws.<region>.s3 and ensure the node subnets route S3 traffic via the endpoint route table. - SSE-KMS with no public egress: KMS requires Interface VPC Endpoint com.amazonaws.<region>.kms; ensure security group allows 443 from exporter pods/nodes. - If customers enforce AWS org SCPs / restrictive egress, confirm both endpoints are present before enabling the sink.

Testing: - terraform fmt + validate - tflint (new files conform to repo rules; suppressed one rule for example-only variables with justification) - Manual apply in sandbox account: verified exporter role can PutObject with SSE-KMS and cannot write unencrypted; verified AccessDenied when missing KMS permissions.

Docs: Updated the S3 sink setup page to explicitly call out at-least-once delivery duplicates and recommend dedupe on event_id (schema v1) rather than object key, since partitions are time-based.

Rollout / Backwards compatibility: This is examples-only + docs; no changes to existing modules used by production stacks. Customers can adopt incrementally.

Commits: - docs: add private endpoint notes for S3/KMS - examples: add siem audit export s3 setup (bucket/kms/iam) - module: add s3_audit_export_bucket helper + README - docs: update S3 sink guide with policy rationale + troubleshooting

Changed files (high level): - examples/siem_audit_export_s3/main.tf (new) - examples/siem_audit_export_s3/variables.tf (new) - examples/siem_audit_export_s3/README.md (new) - modules/s3_audit_export_bucket/main.tf (new) - modules/s3_audit_export_bucket/variables.tf (new) - modules/s3_audit_export_bucket/outputs.tf (new) - modules/s3_audit_export_bucket/README.md (new) - docs/private-endpoints.md (new) - docs/siem-audit-export-s3.md (modified)

Review conversation (selected): Kevin Osei: Can we avoid granting kms:Decrypt by default? For write path it isn’t required, and some customers will be strict about that. Diego Santos: Good call — made decrypt optional behind enable_read_validation var, default false. Also clarified in README why decrypt is not required for PutObject w/ SSE-KMS. Olga Petrov: Please add a sentence on evidence/auditability: who owns the KMS key and how to demonstrate the exporter role access is scoped. Diego Santos: Added “Evidence notes” section with key policy excerpt + suggested AWS Config/Security Hub checks. Colin O'Donnell: Beta customers in Private often use VPC-only clusters; can we add explicit endpoint names + gotchas? Diego Santos: Added S3 gateway endpoint + KMS interface endpoint names, and a checklist for DNS + route tables.

CI: - build (terraform validate): pass - lint (tflint): pass (after update) - docs spellcheck: pass

Outcome: Merged (squash) after approvals from Security + Platform and docs sign-off.
